<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core" xmlns:st="jelly:stapler" xmlns:l="/lib/layout">
  <st:documentation>
    Renders floating buttons in the lower right corner of the page (same style as the scroll buttons of the stage
    view):
    <ul>
      <li>a button to scroll to the top of the page, shown only if the page has been scrolled down,</li>
      <li>buttons to navigate to the previous and next marker of the source code view, together with the position of
      the selected marker (e.g., "3 / 12"), shown only if there are at least two visible markers.</li>
    </ul>
    The buttons are handled by the script of the source code view (SourceCodeViewModel/source-code.js), which also
    provides the keyboard shortcuts 'j' (next marker) and 'k' (previous marker). Hidden markers (e.g., removed by a
    filter of the page) are skipped. This tag is part of the fragment SourceCodeViewModel/content.jelly, so pages
    that embed the source code do not need to add it.
  </st:documentation>

  <div class="prism-navigation jenkins-mobile-hide" aria-hidden="true">
    <button type="button" class="jenkins-button prism-navigation__button prism-navigation__top"
            data-prism-navigation="top" tooltip="${%top}" aria-label="${%top}">
      <l:icon src="symbol-arrow-up-outline plugin-ionicons-api"/>
    </button>
    <div class="prism-navigation__markers">
      <button type="button" class="jenkins-button prism-navigation__button"
              data-prism-navigation="previous" tooltip="${%previous}" aria-label="${%previous}">
        <l:icon src="symbol-chevron-up-outline plugin-ionicons-api"/>
      </button>
      <span class="prism-navigation__position" data-prism-navigation="position" tooltip="${%position}">-</span>
      <button type="button" class="jenkins-button prism-navigation__button"
              data-prism-navigation="next" tooltip="${%next}" aria-label="${%next}">
        <l:icon src="symbol-chevron-down-outline plugin-ionicons-api"/>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</j:jelly>
